# Compat isolate gate

When changing guff analyzer / linter behavior, settings wiring, diagnostic
text, `FromLinter`, positions, or `compat/` harness code, **pass finding-set
parity** before finishing:

```bash
cargo build --release -p guff-lint
./compat/run.sh --isolate --linter <name>   # each touched linter
./compat/run.sh --isolate                   # full suite (114 targets) before handoff
```

## Rules

- Prefer **fixing guff** over adding `compat/isolate/allowlists/` entries.
- Allowlists are last resort for known DEFERRED gaps only.
- New linter → add `compat/isolate/fixtures/<name>/` + `linters.txt` row; keep
  fixtures multi-finding when the linter has multiple rules.
- Do not treat OSS `compat/` alone as sufficient (multi-linter configs hide holes).
- Before claiming perf-safe: `./regress/run.sh` and
  `./regress/run.sh --profile full` on a quiet host (`PERF_GUARD`).

CI runs the full `./compat/run.sh --isolate` suite on every PR / main push
(plus fixture smoke and OSS pr-tier). Agents must still run isolate locally
before handoff so failures are fixed before CI.
